From df72967886d4f95822f5be5e0ef81a61d80c1b41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:15:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 323/377] Unified: "Slides in place", turning in place takes
 the part's fixing away, and both on the bar of a linked part

- "Turns in place" removes the fixing of the part (the first part put in
  is fixed): the angle did not turn the crank and the check only said the
  joint was 90 degrees off (engine field test 0.7.4).
- "Slides in place": a slider joint to the ground along a round face's
  axis (a piston without its cylinder part); a slider needed two parts.
- A round face of a part linked from another file offers both on the bar
  (the bar of a linked part had neither).
- A part shown by a drawing in its own file is still a top of the file:
  "Make Drawing" in a part file with a drawing said there was no part.

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestAssemblySolve, -t TestUnifiedFiles, -t TestContextRules

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
